- op: discuss  # 9139
  at: '2026-04-19T02:17:46Z'  # 9139
  by: agent  # 9139
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9139
  clock: 3  # 9139
  nonce: '9139'  # 9139
  message: "Touches scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh which is a governance file per AGENTS.md. Per the approval workflow protocol, setting needs_human_review and requesting explicit human approval before implementing via auto-pr.\n\nProposed fix (concrete, ready to apply once approved):\n\nscripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh lines ~1060 and ~1106 — change the restore loops to mirror the backup loop's glob pattern:\n\n    # Before (broken — misses hidden files):\n    for f in \"$backup_subdir\"/*; do\n        [[ -f \"$f\" ]] || continue\n        ...\n    done\n\n    # After (matches dotfiles AND regular files):\n    for f in \"$backup_subdir\"/.* \"$backup_subdir\"/*; do\n        [[ -f \"$f\" ]] || continue\n        ...\n    done\n\nThe [[ -f \"$f\" ]] guard is already present and handles the . / .. entries that .* matches. This mirrors the backup loop at line 1024 (`for f in \"$ops_dir\"/.*ops \"$ops_dir\"/*.ops; do`) and requires no shopt dotglob dance.\n\nRegression test plan: add a bash-level test (likely tests/test_auto_pr_rebase_recovery.sh or similar, following existing auto-pr test patterns) that (1) seeds a backup dir with .WI-test-foo.ops.modified containing line INJECTED_FROM_BACKUP, (2) seeds the target with a pre-rebase dotfile containing PRE_EXISTING, (3) calls the patched restore code, (4) asserts the target file contains both lines. Without the fix the test fails (backup-only line missing); with the fix both appear.\n\nRoot cause evidence: hypergumbo_lab_notebook/tracker_ops_loss_04192026_0230.md documents the full timeline and repro of the bash default-glob vs dotglob behavior that caused my 2026-04-19 01:02/01:04/00:47 tracker replies to vanish during auto-pr's rebase-recovery step on the Jackson linker branch."  # 9139
